{% comment %} <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cleanseafoodtoyourdoor.com" crossorigin>
<script src="https://cleanseafoodtoyourdoor.com/core/modals.min.js" async></script> {% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign load_inflektion = true

  if request.page_type == 'page'
    assign announcement_value = page.metafields.custom.enable_announcement_bar.value
    if announcement_value == false
      assign load_inflektion = false
    endif
  endif
-%}

{% if load_inflektion %}
  {%- comment -%}
    preconnect removed 2026-08-09 — Lighthouse: "More than 4 preconnect
    connections were found."

    A preconnect opens a DNS + TCP + TLS handshake immediately, competing for
    the browser's limited early connection budget. That budget should go to
    origins on the critical rendering path: the asset CDN and the font CDN.

    modals.min.js is `async` affiliate tooling — it neither blocks render nor
    paints anything above the fold, so warming its connection ahead of the
    fonts was actively counterproductive. The script still loads exactly as
    before; it just no longer jumps the queue.

    dns-prefetch is deliberately NOT used as a substitute. It carries its own
    (smaller) cost and this origin does not need the head start.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="https://cleanseafoodtoyourdoor.com/core/modals.min.js" async></script>
{% endif %}